Article 2 (Designation and Modification)
(1) The head of a school seeking designation as a school at which academic qualifications for admission or transfer admission to higher-level schools are recognized (hereinafter referred to as "designation") shall apply at least six months before the beginning of the academic year, according to the following classification: [Amended on January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; and March 23, 2013.]
1. A school falling under any subparagraph of Article 2 of the Elementary and Secondary Education Act: Apply to the Superintendent of Education, accompanied by the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Elementary and Secondary Education Act;
2. A school falling under any subparagraph of Article 2 of the Higher Education Act: Apply to the Minister of Education, accompanied by the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Higher Education Act.
(2) The Minister of Education or Superintendent of Education shall notify the applicant of the results within three months from the date of receipt of the application under paragraph (1). [Amended on January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; and March 23, 2013.]
(3) Where a school intends to modify matters designated under paragraph (1), the head of a school referred to in paragraph (1) 1 shall apply to the Superintendent of Education, and the head of a school referred to in paragraph (1) 2 shall apply to the Minister of Education, accompanied by documents stating the following matters: [Amended on January 31, 2001; March 4, 2008; and March 23, 2013.]
1. Reasons for the modification;
2. Matters to be modified;
3. Date of the modification.
